ites [:critique_notes], :output-schemas {:critique_notes :string}}] [:llm {:instruction \"Produce the final comprehensive unit plan by revising the draft based on the critique. \\n                       Ensure the output is a polished, professional document for a course syllabus.\\n                       Required structure per session: \\n                       - Session Title & Objectives\\n                       - Timed Breakdown (90 mins total)\\n                       - Materials Needed (Projector/Whiteboard/Pasos 1)\\n                       - Formative Assessment Method.\", :reads [:draft_plan :critique_notes], :writes [:result], :output-schemas {:result :string}}] [:final {:keys [:result]}]]\n      ```\n    - Reads: (none declared) · Writes: :draft_plan, :critique_notes, :result · Outputs: :result — rebind these keys to your task's blackboard; the logic stays as written.\n\nRepresentative uses (concrete tasks this pattern has shipped on):\n  - INSTRUCTION:\n\nDevelop an 8-session lesson sequence for a Beginner Spanish adult evening course using the attached A1 learning objectives. Each session is 90 minutes. Resources available include a projector, whiteboards, and the 'Pasos 1' coursebook. For each session, list specific objectives, a timed breakdown of communicative activities, required materials, and a quick formative assessment method. Prioritize practical conversational skills, specifically ordering food, asking for directions, and shopping. Ensure a logical progression suited for adult learners with minimal out-of-class study time. Deliver a comprehensive unit plan only; no individual worksheets required.\n\nREADS: (none)\nWRITES: :result\nMCP-TOOLS: (none)\nBROWSER-TOOLS: (none)\n\n### Behavioral competencies (top 2 from corpus retrieval)\n1. Behavioral: Design (confidence: 0.95)\n   Why this fits: The task is to develop a comprehensive unit plan (design) from specific constraints (8 sessions, 90 mins, adult learners) and learning objectives. This candi