t (confidence 0.70, evidence-count 1)\n    - Avoid when: the task pairs a speed target with an output-invariance constraint\n    - Recommended fix: measure first (profile/timing), change only the proven hot path, then compare optimized output to the baseline before committing\n\n  - **Failure mode:** guessing the bottleneck from reading the code instead of profiling wastes the edit on the wrong region and often misses the real cost (I/O, N+1, allocation) entirely (confidence 0.70, evidence-count 1)\n    - Avoid when: a profiler or representative-input timing harness is available\n    - Recommended fix: always derive the hot path from a measurement stage; let the profile, not intuition, choose where to edit\n\nRepresentative uses (concrete tasks this pattern has shipped on):\n  - the report-rendering endpoint is slow on large inputs; profile it and optimize the hot path so a 10k-row report renders under 500ms without changing the output\n  - a nightly aggregation job exceeds its window; find and fix the dominant cost while keeping the produced totals identical\n\n   Adopt / adapt / SPECIALIZE / mint-adjacent — use the evidence above, not the score alone:\n   - ADOPT this pattern as-is if it is an EXACT fit for your task.\n   - ADAPT it (keep the shape, override the specifics) if it mostly fits.\n   - SPECIALIZE — if this is a BROAD fit rather than an exact one (its `:summary`/strengths describe a more general shape than your task, or its `:avoid-when` flags your context), mint a domain-specialized CHILD of THIS behavior. The child keeps the parent's proven shape but pins your domain, gets a STABLE derived id, and ACCRUES evidence under the parent (it is retrievable on subsequent classify-behaviors calls):\n\n       (mint-behavior! \"<short-kebab-name>\"\n                       {:capabilities [\"<concrete action verb + object>\"]\n                        :strengths [{:trait \"<what works AND why>\"\n                                     :good-when \"<context guard>\"\n